NOTE = '''0.4.16 (2026-10-23) = THE HATCH REELS ALWAYS FINISH + A REAL DOG / CORGI PICTURE (Skyy's test of 0.4.15):
  A. Skyy (screenshot of Character > Pets > HATCHING, Mythic Mining Egg: THE PET reel on Warthog, ITS RARITY an empty gold square + "?",
     the footer "Rolling... Skip (or Esc) shows the result at once."): "roll bugged and froze". The hatch itself had gone through (the
     server log: "You hatched a Mythic Warthog from your Mythic Mining Egg!") - only the page's two-reel animation stopped in reel 1.
     CAUSE: the reel is a chain of one-shot tasks (the server scheduler -> PetWorld.execute(the world cached at the start) -> tick -> the
     next task). Every link could drop the chain WITHOUT a fallback: a failed world hop only bumped gen (the page stayed on "Rolling..."
     forever), anything thrown in tick outside its draw try (sounds, delays, the reveal) was swallowed by PetReel.run, and nothing ever
     checked that the roll reached its end. The rarity reel was also drawn as 5 EMPTY cells + "?" while reel 1 spins - the "empty gold
     square" of the screenshot is that waiting state, not a missing Mythic picture (all six rarity tokens have their gem icons).
     1. Every frame re-reads the player's CURRENT world from the PlayerRef (the cached one is the fallback) - PetHatchPage.hop.
     2. tick = a guard + step() inside one try: anything thrown = the result card at once (PetHatchPage.finish: ONE rebuild + the reveal).
     3. A WATCHDOG per roll (PetReel.dog): scheduled at the start for the roll's own length (expectMs = the frame delays + both holds) + the
        new Server Setup row pets.hatch.stallSeconds (int 1-60 s, default 5, adv). If that roll is still spinning then, the result card is
        shown (one WARN per server run); a frame that comes after the deadline does the same. A roll that ended normally makes it a no-op.
     4. A world hop that fails stops the chain; the page then finishes on the next click (Skip / Esc / a tab) and the chat line still comes
        from the record within 30 s (PetEgg.unseen, unchanged).
     5. While reel 1 spins, reel 2 shows its first five rarity pictures (gems with the rarity colour) + "?" instead of empty cells.
     Skip / Esc / the tabs keep jumping to the result (one packet per click). The hatch itself (PetHatchery.hatch / PetEgg, the item, the
     pet record, hatch.unseen) is untouched.
  B. Skyy: "the dog still shows up as a sword". Dog and Corgi have no vanilla model icon, so since 0.4.0 their portrait items
     (Skyy_PetIcon_Dog / _Corgi, also used by SkyyWardrobe's Requip) pointed at their skill's TOOL icon (Combat = a sword, Farming = a hoe).
     Now both portraits are RENDERED at build time from the vanilla pet model + texture (Server/Models/Pets/Dog.json / Corgi.json ->
     tools/skyyart.render_icon, 128 px fitted, halved to 64 like the other portraits; nothing vanilla-derived in git). Every other kind
     already had a creature picture (vanilla ModelsGenerated icons; dragons = the recoloured Dragon_Frost icon). The starter choice page
     shows the pet portraits too (it showed the skill tool icons - the Dog = a sword).
  SAVED DATA: none. New Server Setup row pets.hatch.stallSeconds. FLOOR (rollback): rolls back alone to 0.4.15 (the row is ignored, Dog /
  Corgi show their tool icons again, the reel can freeze again). The 0.4.15 / 0.4.11 floors stand.
'''

